py's output leaves the other copy's output at its prior. Since the other copy gets a different input, it is a separate node, and I'm checking whether it depends on mine at all. The essay treats the two as distinct nodes, so intervening on one leaves the other fixed.\n\nUnder A-FDT, the other copy's node is separate from mine, and the essay's red/blue case holds it at its prior when I intervene. Only the names and leads differ, so I'll treat the inputs as distinct and conclude that submitting is the answer.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Working under A-FDT as the essay reads it: this is a twin prisoner's dilemma with different inputs, so intervening on my copy's output leaves the other copy's output at its prior. Since the other copy gets a different input, it is a separate node, and I'm checking whether it depends on mine at all. The essay treats the two as distinct nodes, so intervening on one leaves the other fixed.\n\nUnder A-FDT, the other copy's node is separate from mine, and the essay's red/blue case holds it at its prior when I intervene. Only the names and leads differ, so I'll treat the inputs as distinct and conclude that submitting is the answer.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9628,"completion_tokens":824,"total_tokens":10452,"cost":0.054992,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.054992,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.038512,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.01648},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":281,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}